{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir","id":322820,"title":"About Iminir","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-26T08:32:54-08:00","id":322820,"title":"About Iminir","content":"So, will most of Iminir hate Sin-Eaters as oWoD Garou hated vamires?<br /> Cuz for it is quite bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T09:14:43-08:00","id":322872,"title":"","content":"I think the point of that stereotype is less &quot;We should hunt the Sin-Eaters&quot; and more &quot;Alien ephemeral being riding co-pilot in a mortal and giving them strange powers and transformations? Sounds like a Claimed to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Imnir should see Sin-Eaters as similar to what they hunt, which should cause a little bit of mistrust. But so long as the Sin-Eater isn't screwing with the Gauntlet or causing problems in the Imnir's neighbourhood, it shouldn't be too antagonistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T10:17:53-08:00","id":322945,"title":"","content":"I think there will be some Iminir who make it a point to kill Sin-Eaters. But that's going to be as widespread as some Iron Masters who make it a point to kill Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T10:54:37-08:00","id":322974,"title":"","content":"Stereotypes always seemed to depict how the 'average' member of a splat feels about certain things. Playing and non-playing characters are free to be different, as it's just a stereotype, and not an enforced belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-26-2014, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T11:09:30-08:00","id":322984,"title":"","content":"The Farsil Luhal won't perceive *all* people as their prey, so there's no reason to believe that the Iminir hunt everything that smells like a Ridden.<br /> <br /> Besides that, crossover is bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T11:15:17-08:00","id":322989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir?p=322974#post322974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stereotypes always seemed like how the 'average' member of a splat feels about certain things. Playing and non-playing characters are free to be different, as it's just a stereotype, and not an enforced belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but at some point you have to ask &quot;Why are we so different?&quot; And of course, if you don't care about what an average group member thinks, what's the point of making your character a member of that group?<br /> <br /> In this particular instance, it's important to know that Iminir probably don't <i>generally</i> attack Sin-Eaters on sight, just that they notice the similarities between Sin-Eaters and Claimed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T11:16:04-08:00","id":322991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir?p=322984#post322984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Besides that, crossover is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey now, no reason to make sweeping generalizations like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T16:04:30-08:00","id":323223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir?p=322984#post322984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Farsil Luhal won't perceive *all* people as their prey, so there's no reason to believe that the Iminir hunt everything that smells like a Ridden.<br /> <br /> Besides that, crossover is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>This basically. QFT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T16:20:31-08:00","id":323226,"title":"","content":"Bone Shadows, Iron Masters, and Blood Talons don't hunt every single spirit, human, or werewolf they run across respectively. They hold that in reserve for trouble makers, though I can imagine they make it a point to find targets rather than just waiting around for them to show up if they're taking their job seriously. Storm Lords and Hunters in Darkness, however, don't have the same problem; Hosts and Ridden seem to be ubiquitously intolerable.<br /> <br /> I can see, easily, how an Iminir would look at a Sin-Eater and mistake it for some kind of exotic Ridden. A particularly wise Iminir might know the difference and give the Sin-Eater a pass, but given that it's a sacred oath and the tendency for Uratha to follow their instincts this seems like it'd be the exception to the rule. When zoomed out, I would imagine that Iminir are considerably more aggressive to Sin-Eaters than any of the other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T02:50:42-08:00","id":323552,"title":"","content":"I think it should also be noted that in the Geist: the Sin-Eaters core book it mentions that while Werewolves acknowledge that Ghosts do exist and act very similar to Spirits in form an ability they stand outside the preview of Werewolves for the most part. With that logic one could assume that the Storm Lords are just as likely to hunt Sin-Eaters as much as they would call the Siskur-Dah on any mortal Ridden or Claimed by an ordinary Ghost, which would be only under special circumstances (like if the Pact's territory or Wolf-Blooded were being targeted by the malicious Specter.) That being said Geists themselves are even more similar to Spirits than normal Ghosts are so it would probably be harder for the Uratha to tell the difference between a Sin-Eater and one of the Spirit Claimed, except of course when the Sin-Eater comes back to life (which that alone would make for a wonderful plot twist).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T05:29:28-08:00","id":330039,"title":"","content":"This also made me think that we are in the World of Darkness, after all, so the stereotypes and generalities people hold to are pretty, well, dark. The only game where you can expect the NPC's to be even more of a mess, internally, than the PC's!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:27:24-08:00","id":330501,"title":"","content":"It's bad. Look like OWoD Garou nazism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T23:03:50-08:00","id":331986,"title":"","content":"Well from what I have read so far it seems like each Tribe of the Moon's culture revolves around hunting a specific prey. However, how they hunt that prey and what they do with it once it's been captured is entirely dependent on the individual Pack's traditions and the mentality of their own Totem. For instance a Pack of Storm Lords might successfully hunt a Ridden mortal and bind the individual far from the Spirit's resonate energy and perform a ritual that exorcises the Spirit from it's mortal host to honor a Totem related to rehabilitation or starvation. After all hunting lone Spirits are the preview of the Bone Shadow's anyway so it's not their custom to hunt a Spirit once it's no longer riding a human or beast. So some may consider Sin-Eaters to be a form of Claimed and hunt them like any other Spiritual abomination, while another would consider them foreign creatures that would best be avoided so long as they remain off the Pack's territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T05:36:45-08:00","id":332161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir?p=330501#post330501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's bad. Look like OWoD Garou nazism.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's, um, a bit extreme, don't you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T14:38:27-08:00","id":332507,"title":"","content":"Hm-m... no? Cuz Sin-Eaters and werewolves are almost natural allies. They can be useful for each other, cuz their enemy are quite similar. But Iminir too stubborn for try to understand the difference between SE and Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T16:11:25-08:00","id":332529,"title":"","content":"What we know merely implies that the average Iminir would, in absence of a proper frame of reference, mistake a Sin Eater for a Claimed. There's nothing that suggests they are too stubborn to understand the difference given the right information nor that they would enforce the &quot;Wyrmspawn, kill on sight!&quot; policy the Garou generally had for vampires.<br /> <br /> Hunting a prey does not merely mean to kill it immediately as soon as it approaches, it often involves knowing the prey a bit and there's absolutely no kind of compulsion that forces any Uratha of any Tribe to do so.<br /> <br /> I would also say that, even in their usual fanaticism, the CWoD wolves were a bit justified in their attitude against vampires considering the CWoD setting and history and that calling it nazism is a little too much (I won't deny it was unsavory and and closed-minded, especially from a &quot;nice&quot; vampire point of view) but that's another can of worms that does not belong to this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 12-06-2014, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T17:43:45-08:00","id":332611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir?p=332507#post332507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cuz Sin-Eaters and werewolves are almost natural allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T21:39:00-08:00","id":332743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir?p=332611#post332611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes you think that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would venture to guess it's because their roles are fairly similar from an outsider's perspective. Or at least they were in 1E. Werewolves policed the boundary between the Material and the Shadow, Sin-Eaters performed a similar job with ghosts and the underworld. It's not a one to one comparison, but in theory if they both had enough context to piece it together they might consider each other as 'on the same side' as it were.<br /> <br /> That said neither splat knows much about the other and aren't prone to sitting down and really hashing out the details, so that point is kind of moot. Even in a big crossover game like the one I'm helping to run, that kind of detail just doesn't come up much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T22:41:39-08:00","id":332763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir?p=332743#post332743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would venture to guess it's because their roles are fairly similar from an outsider's perspective. Or at least they were in 1E. Werewolves policed the boundary between the Material and the Shadow, Sin-Eaters performed a similar job with ghosts and the underworld. It's not a one to one comparison, but in theory if they both had enough context to piece it together they might consider each other as 'on the same side' as it were.<br /> <br /> That said neither splat knows much about the other and aren't prone to sitting down and really hashing out the details, so that point is kind of moot. Even in a big crossover game like the one I'm helping to run, that kind of detail just doesn't come up much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, as I've pointed out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/286719-fwc-preview-terra-incognita?p=287004#post287004\">elsewhere</a>, the Underworld and the Shadow <i>really</i> aren't terribly interchangeable and ghosts and the Bound are a veritable Babel of conflicting roles and origin stories unto themselves; over half the Archetypes barely need squinted at to see them turned to ends that are in many ways the <i>complete opposite</i> of what the Uratha do (to say nothing of the shared-culture-such-as-it-is actually having a nomenclatural distinction between &quot;folks who see a duty to the dead&quot; and &quot;folks who don't see such a duty&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T23:09:07-08:00","id":332779,"title":"","content":"Then again, not every Uratha and Sin-Eater is cut from the same cloth. A Reaper who hunts Abmortals who've long outlived their life might be held in high regard by a Werewolf, most likely an Iron Master or Bone Shadow, who's sacred prey mirrors the Sin-Eater's. That same Reaper might be held in disgust by another Uratha simply because, &quot;That bloodthirsty freak is a total hypocrite. Our way is a sacred task. Their's is the caprice of a Death Spirit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not every Sin-Eater is good. And not every Uratha gives a damn whether they are or not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T00:07:03-08:00","id":332841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/322820-about-iminir?p=330501#post330501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's bad. Look like OWoD Garou nazism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's your solution have each and every Forsaken be given a copy of Geist: The sin Eaters in universe so they can have perfect out of universe knowledge rather than you being like normal people and basing out of context things(which a sineater generally is) on previous information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T06:00:30-08:00","id":332920,"title":"","content":"While the roles of Sin Eaters and Uratha might seem to have parallels, as far as I know, Shadow and Underworld are mutually exclusive. Cue in the Lodge of Death and you have Uratha who'd like nothing more than vivisect Sin Eaters in order to coax the Geist to Gift them with ways to open portals to the Underworld, cue in the Lodge of Cerberus and you'll have more than likely a group of religious fanatics after the hybrid. And those aren't even Iminir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T07:01:03-08:00","id":332943,"title":"","content":"So, <i>Iminir </i>and the Sin-Eaters. I actually wrote a big, long post on this but it basically boils down to how the individual Sin-Eater is acting and how the Storyteller rules certain Gifts etc interact with Sin-Eaters as to whether Storm Lords will determine that the Bound is actually just a Claimed or that it's something meaningfully different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}